WEBVTT

00:00:11.873 --> 00:00:13.698
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:15.943
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:15.944 --> 00:00:17.258
The family business.

00:00:22.082 --> 00:00:23.543
You're planning on bringing
the demon here, aren't you?

00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:25.883
Having some stupid, macho showdown?!

00:00:25.884 --> 00:00:27.213
I have a plan, Sam.

00:00:27.214 --> 00:00:29.590
Dean is dying, and you have a plan!

00:00:29.591 --> 00:00:30.886
I won't hunt this demon,

00:00:30.887 --> 00:00:33.041
Not until we know Dean's okay.

00:00:33.235 --> 00:00:35.520
Did you really think you could trap me?

00:00:35.522 --> 00:00:37.845
Oh, I don't want to trap
you. I want to make a deal.

00:00:37.844 --> 00:00:39.776
I will give you the colt and the bullet,

00:00:39.778 --> 00:00:41.136
But you got to help Dean.

00:00:41.139 --> 00:00:42.491
You got to bring him back.

00:00:42.495 --> 00:00:45.021
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:00:45.026 --> 00:00:47.653
Giving to Salomon, these protective
circles, they really work.

00:00:47.657 --> 00:00:50.701
You get a demon in one,
they're trapped, powerless.

00:03:31.688 --> 00:03:33.501
What's going on? Oh, my god.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.002
Get a doctor.

00:03:38.146 --> 00:03:39.423
Run!

00:03:41.168 --> 00:03:42.263
What happened?

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.812
Talk to me. Dogs.

00:03:43.827 --> 00:03:46.672
Stay with us, baby! Dogs... Black dogs.

00:03:47.836 --> 00:03:48.783
Robert?

00:03:49.226 --> 00:03:51.141
Robert, don't you die on me!

00:04:06.528 --> 00:04:08.192
So much for our low profile.

00:04:08.277 --> 00:04:11.530
You got a warrant in St. Louis, and now
you're officially in the feds' database.

00:04:11.545 --> 00:04:14.043
Dude, I'm like Dillinger or
something. Dean, it's not funny.

00:04:14.335 --> 00:04:16.401
It makes the job harder. We
got to be more careful now.

00:04:16.408 --> 00:04:17.523
What do they got on you?

00:04:20.158 --> 00:04:21.073
I'm sure they just

00:04:21.177 --> 00:04:23.620
Haven't posted it yet.
Well, you're no accessory,

00:04:23.677 --> 00:04:24.942
Nothing? Shut up.

00:04:26.078 --> 00:04:27.622
You're jealous. No, I'm not!

00:04:27.627 --> 00:04:28.363
Uh-Huh.

00:04:30.277 --> 00:04:31.022
All right,

00:04:31.135 --> 00:04:34.051
What do you got on the case there,
you innocent, harmless young man, you?

00:04:37.455 --> 00:04:41.151
"Architect Sean Boyden plummeted to
his death from the roof of his home,

00:04:41.156 --> 00:04:42.873
A condominium he designed"

00:04:43.368 --> 00:04:45.923
Build a high rise and
jump off. That's classy.

00:04:46.115 --> 00:04:47.513
When did he call animal control?

00:04:47.515 --> 00:04:48.593
Two days earlier.

00:04:48.596 --> 00:04:50.382
Did he actually say "black dog"? Yeah.

00:04:50.388 --> 00:04:52.733
"Vicious, wild, black dog"

00:04:52.897 --> 00:04:55.743
The authorities couldn't find
it, and no one else saw it.

00:04:55.988 --> 00:04:59.231
In fact, the authorities are a
little confused as to how a wild dog

00:04:59.237 --> 00:05:00.533
Could get past the doorman,

00:05:00.536 --> 00:05:03.853
Take the elevator up, and start roaming
the halls of the cushiest joint in town.

00:05:03.988 --> 00:05:07.062
After that, no more calls.
He doesn't show up for work.

00:05:07.386 --> 00:05:09.071
Two days later, he takes a swan dive.

00:05:09.077 --> 00:05:10.972
You think we're dealing
with an actual black dog?

00:05:11.195 --> 00:05:13.281
Well, maybe. What's the lore on it?

00:05:13.285 --> 00:05:14.601
It's all pretty vague.

00:05:14.748 --> 00:05:17.252
There are spectral black
dogs all over the world, but

00:05:17.396 --> 00:05:20.020
Some say they're animal
spirits, others say death omens.

00:05:20.026 --> 00:05:21.523
But anyways, whatever they are, they're

00:05:21.885 --> 00:05:23.112
Big, nasty...

00:05:23.117 --> 00:05:25.431
Yeah, bet they could hump
the crap out of your leg.

00:05:25.437 --> 00:05:26.561
Look at that one. Huh?

00:05:28.526 --> 00:05:29.370
What? They could.

00:05:32.628 --> 00:05:33.441
So,

00:05:34.016 --> 00:05:36.452
You and Sean Boyden were
business partners for

00:05:36.946 --> 00:05:38.380
Almost 10 years, right?

00:05:38.698 --> 00:05:39.632
That's right.

00:05:39.635 --> 00:05:42.241
Now, one more time, this is
for... A tribute for Mr. Boyden,

00:05:42.247 --> 00:05:43.522
"Architectural Digest".

00:05:46.708 --> 00:05:48.320
Funny to you? No,

00:05:49.336 --> 00:05:50.193
It's just uh

00:05:50.357 --> 00:05:51.522
"Tribute".

00:05:52.356 --> 00:05:53.411
Yeah.

00:05:53.435 --> 00:05:55.503
See, Sean always got the tributes.

00:05:56.948 --> 00:05:58.213
He kills himself,

00:05:58.885 --> 00:06:00.552
Leaves me and his family behind,

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:02.552
But he gets another tribute.

00:06:02.678 --> 00:06:03.523
Right.

00:06:04.696 --> 00:06:06.581
Any idea why he'd do such a thing?

00:06:07.176 --> 00:06:09.463
I have no clue. I mean,
he lived a charmed life.

00:06:09.876 --> 00:06:10.783
How so?

00:06:11.238 --> 00:06:12.803
He was a flat-Out genius.

00:06:13.085 --> 00:06:15.372
I mean, I'm capable,
but, next to him, uh...

00:06:16.738 --> 00:06:18.450
It wasn't always that way either.

00:06:18.617 --> 00:06:19.461
No?

00:06:20.968 --> 00:06:22.353
You  want to know the truth?

00:06:22.605 --> 00:06:25.053
There was a time where he
couldn't even design a pup tent.

00:06:25.208 --> 00:06:28.240
Hell, 10 years ago, he was working
as a bartender at this place called

00:06:28.438 --> 00:06:29.330
Lloyd's,

00:06:29.477 --> 00:06:30.720
A complete dive.

00:06:30.948 --> 00:06:32.731
So, what changed? You got me.

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:33.932
But overnight

00:06:34.288 --> 00:06:35.842
He gets this huge commission,

00:06:35.966 --> 00:06:37.393
And he starts designing...

00:06:38.777 --> 00:06:40.263
He starts designing the most

00:06:40.437 --> 00:06:41.870
Ingenious buildings

00:06:41.888 --> 00:06:43.980
Anyone has ever seen. It was like

00:06:44.135 --> 00:06:46.823
The level of Van Gogh and Mozart.

00:06:47.788 --> 00:06:48.523
What?

00:06:48.527 --> 00:06:49.743
It's funny.

00:06:49.787 --> 00:06:51.153
True geniuses, they...

00:06:51.615 --> 00:06:53.251
Seem to die young, don't they?

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:56.471
To have

00:06:56.476 --> 00:06:58.641
That kind of talent...

00:06:58.986 --> 00:06:59.841
Why...

00:07:01.458 --> 00:07:02.762
Why just throw it away?

00:07:14.078 --> 00:07:14.912
So?

00:07:15.238 --> 00:07:16.980
The secretary's name is Carly.

00:07:17.418 --> 00:07:19.342
She's 23. She kayaks...

00:07:19.678 --> 00:07:20.491
And they're real.

00:07:20.497 --> 00:07:23.682
You didn't happen to ask her if she's
seen any black dogs lately, did you?

00:07:23.685 --> 00:07:25.183
Every complain called in this week

00:07:25.186 --> 00:07:28.402
About anything big, black, or
dog like. There's 19 calls in all,

00:07:28.407 --> 00:07:29.561
And, uh,

00:07:30.906 --> 00:07:31.982
I don't know what this is.

00:07:34.608 --> 00:07:36.121
You mean, Carly's my space address?

00:07:36.125 --> 00:07:37.443
Yeah, my space. What the hell is that?

00:07:39.377 --> 00:07:41.141
Seriously, is that like
some sort of porn site?

00:07:45.866 --> 00:07:48.093
I swear, if this is
another freakin' pomeranian

00:07:48.098 --> 00:07:49.830
Barking in the neighbor's yard...

00:07:50.556 --> 00:07:51.780
Afternoon, ma'am.

00:07:52.458 --> 00:07:53.461
Animal control.

00:07:54.076 --> 00:07:55.920
Oh, someone already came yesterday.

00:07:55.925 --> 00:07:57.180
Oh, we're just following up.

00:07:57.617 --> 00:07:59.482
We're looking for Dr. Sylvia Perlman.

00:08:01.026 --> 00:08:01.942
The  doctor,

00:08:01.956 --> 00:08:03.081
Well, she...

00:08:03.598 --> 00:08:06.260
I don't know exactly when she'll
be back. She left two days ago.

00:08:06.307 --> 00:08:07.140
Okay.

00:08:07.177 --> 00:08:08.101
And you are?

00:08:08.146 --> 00:08:09.230
I'm Miss Perlman's maid.

00:08:09.235 --> 00:08:10.500
So, where did the doctor go?

00:08:10.505 --> 00:08:11.371
I'm not sure.

00:08:11.687 --> 00:08:13.873
She just packed and went.
She didn't say where.

00:08:14.215 --> 00:08:15.993
That stray dog, did you find it finally?

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:17.451
Uh, not yet.

00:08:17.635 --> 00:08:18.480
You know,

00:08:18.486 --> 00:08:21.062
You didn't ever happen to
see the dog yourself, did you?

00:08:21.355 --> 00:08:24.083
Well, no. I never even heard it.

00:08:24.355 --> 00:08:27.111
I was almost starting to think the
doctor was imagining things, but

00:08:27.118 --> 00:08:29.932
She's not like that, so...
You know, I read she was

00:08:29.936 --> 00:08:31.603
The chief surgeon at the hospital.

00:08:32.026 --> 00:08:35.010
So she's got to be, what, 42, 43?
That's pretty young for that job.

00:08:35.015 --> 00:08:36.490
Youngest in the history of the place.

00:08:36.672 --> 00:08:38.745
She got the position 10 years ago.

00:08:41.084 --> 00:08:43.396
An overnight success, 10 years ago.

00:08:43.588 --> 00:08:44.996
Yeah, we know a guy like that.

00:08:46.209 --> 00:08:47.382
Oh, look at this.

00:08:51.056 --> 00:08:52.040
Lloyd's bar.

00:09:19.976 --> 00:09:21.053
Miss Perlman?

00:09:21.805 --> 00:09:23.340
I've been calling for hours!

00:09:23.607 --> 00:09:26.703
You need to vacate the room,
or you got to pay for the night!

00:09:30.665 --> 00:09:31.591
Okay,

00:09:31.715 --> 00:09:32.713
No problem.

00:10:14.535 --> 00:10:15.621
H ey.

00:10:16.415 --> 00:10:17.201
Yeah?

00:10:18.085 --> 00:10:19.101
That's weird.

00:10:19.838 --> 00:10:21.783
What? Think someone planted these?

00:10:25.495 --> 00:10:26.941
In the middle of all these weeds?

00:10:27.307 --> 00:10:28.770
These are, uh, what do you call them?

00:10:28.778 --> 00:10:30.152
Yarrow flowers? Yeah.

00:10:30.155 --> 00:10:31.921
Used for certain rituals, aren't they?

00:10:32.286 --> 00:10:34.572
Yeah, actually, summoning rituals.

00:10:37.498 --> 00:10:38.270
So,

00:10:38.875 --> 00:10:41.902
Two people become sudden
successes about 10 years ago,

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:44.040
Right around the time they were
hanging out here at Lloyd's.

00:10:44.056 --> 00:10:45.933
Where there just happens
to be a crossroads.

00:10:46.008 --> 00:10:47.502
You think? Let's find out.

00:10:54.415 --> 00:10:55.913
Seem about the dead center to you?

00:11:03.336 --> 00:11:04.190
Yahtzee.

00:11:19.448 --> 00:11:21.401
I'd be willing to bet
that's graveyard dirt.

00:11:22.907 --> 00:11:26.720
And a black cat bone.
That's serious spellwork.

00:11:27.076 --> 00:11:28.820
I mean, that's deep south hoodoo stuff.

00:11:28.835 --> 00:11:30.653
Used to summon a demon.

00:11:31.785 --> 00:11:33.170
Not just summon one.

00:11:34.066 --> 00:11:35.833
Crossroad's where pacts are made.

00:11:36.686 --> 00:11:39.562
These people are actually making
deals with the damned thing.

00:11:40.066 --> 00:11:41.582
You know, 'cause that always ends good.

00:11:43.167 --> 00:11:44.703
They're seeing dogs, all right...

00:11:45.695 --> 00:11:48.123
But not black dogs.
They're seeing hellhounds,

00:11:48.556 --> 00:11:50.261
Demonic pit bulls.

00:11:50.266 --> 00:11:53.332
Whoever this demon is, it's
back and it's collecting.

00:11:53.505 --> 00:11:55.951
And that doctor lady,
wherever she's running,

00:11:56.595 --> 00:11:58.271
She ain't running fast enough.

00:13:20.647 --> 00:13:21.800
Holy...

00:13:22.115 --> 00:13:23.260
Holy?

00:13:26.736 --> 00:13:27.863
Guess again.

00:13:28.438 --> 00:13:31.290
<i>Now save poor bob, if you please</i>

00:13:34.846 --> 00:13:36.552
I want to play guitar.

00:13:37.687 --> 00:13:40.572
I want you to make me the
best blues man ever lived.

00:13:41.927 --> 00:13:43.551
If that's what you want...

00:13:47.498 --> 00:13:48.302
So...

00:13:48.787 --> 00:13:49.760
How...

00:13:50.155 --> 00:13:51.420
Do we shake on it?

00:14:21.487 --> 00:14:23.880
So, it's just like the
Robert Johnson legend, right?

00:14:24.297 --> 00:14:26.583
I mean, "selling your soul at the
crossroads", that kind of deal?

00:14:26.586 --> 00:14:28.071
Except that wasn't a legend.

00:14:28.147 --> 00:14:29.511
You know his music.

00:14:31.277 --> 00:14:32.821
You don't know Robert Johnson songs?

00:14:33.096 --> 00:14:35.741
Sam, there's occult
references all over his lyrics.

00:14:35.755 --> 00:14:37.381
I mean, "Crossroad blues,"

00:14:37.618 --> 00:14:38.970
"Me and the Devil blues,"

00:14:38.978 --> 00:14:40.402
"Hellhound on my Trail"?

00:14:42.496 --> 00:14:44.750
Story  goes that he died
choking on his own blood.

00:14:44.755 --> 00:14:48.493
He was hallucinating and
muttering about big, evil dogs.

00:14:49.338 --> 00:14:50.830
And now it's happening all over again.

00:14:50.838 --> 00:14:51.682
Yeah.

00:14:51.827 --> 00:14:54.593
We got to find out if anyone else
struck any bargains around here.

00:14:54.697 --> 00:14:55.540
Right,

00:14:55.546 --> 00:14:57.352
So, we got to clean up
these people's mess for them?

00:14:57.356 --> 00:14:59.312
They're not exactly squeaky-Clean.

00:14:59.517 --> 00:15:02.191
Nobody put a gun to their head and
forced them to play "let's make a deal".

00:15:02.197 --> 00:15:03.991
So, what, we should
just leave them to die?

00:15:03.997 --> 00:15:06.710
Somebody goes over Niagara in a barrel,
you gonna jump in to try to save them?

00:15:06.715 --> 00:15:07.483
Dean...

00:15:09.467 --> 00:15:10.261
All right...

00:15:11.047 --> 00:15:12.073
Fine.

00:15:13.705 --> 00:15:16.200
Rituals like this, you got to put
your own photo into the mix, right?

00:15:16.205 --> 00:15:18.371
So this guy probably summoned the thing.

00:15:18.487 --> 00:15:20.312
Let's see if anyone inside knows him...

00:15:21.216 --> 00:15:22.250
If he's still alive.

00:15:30.368 --> 00:15:32.552
What's this guy's name,
again? George Darrow.

00:15:32.556 --> 00:15:34.730
Apparent quite the regular at Lloyd's.

00:15:35.688 --> 00:15:39.270
This house probably ain't up
next on "mtv cribs", is it?

00:15:39.277 --> 00:15:40.233
Yeah.

00:15:40.235 --> 00:15:41.841
So, whatever kind of deal he made...

00:15:41.856 --> 00:15:43.182
Wasn't for cash.

00:15:43.417 --> 00:15:46.593
Ah, who knows? Maybe his place is
full of babes in princess Leia bikinis.

00:15:48.018 --> 00:15:49.392
I'm just saying,

00:15:49.408 --> 00:15:51.883
This guy's got one epic bill come due.

00:15:52.175 --> 00:15:54.001
Hope at least he asked
for something fun.

00:16:00.848 --> 00:16:01.781
Look at that.

00:16:08.346 --> 00:16:09.402
What is that, pepper?

00:16:13.288 --> 00:16:15.240
Who the hell are you? George Darrow?

00:16:15.858 --> 00:16:17.512
I'm not buying anything.
Whoa, looks like

00:16:17.606 --> 00:16:19.081
You  went for the wrong shaker, there.

00:16:19.956 --> 00:16:22.590
Usually, when you want to keep
something evil out, you go for the salt.

00:16:25.175 --> 00:16:26.740
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:16:26.966 --> 00:16:28.110
Talking about this.

00:16:32.007 --> 00:16:33.103
Tell me...

00:16:33.308 --> 00:16:34.690
You seen that hellhound yet?

00:16:35.346 --> 00:16:36.151
Look,

00:16:36.758 --> 00:16:37.610
We want to help.

00:16:37.617 --> 00:16:38.763
Please,

00:16:39.318 --> 00:16:40.491
Just 5 minutes.

00:16:53.838 --> 00:16:55.491
So, what is that stuff out front?

00:16:55.885 --> 00:16:57.170
Goofer dust.

00:16:59.958 --> 00:17:03.613
What, you boys think you know something
about something, but not goofer dust?

00:17:08.905 --> 00:17:11.140
Well, we know a little
about a lot of things,

00:17:11.145 --> 00:17:13.041
Just enough to make us dangerous.

00:17:13.997 --> 00:17:14.930
What is it?

00:17:15.427 --> 00:17:16.321
Hoodoo.

00:17:17.405 --> 00:17:18.822
My grandma taught me.

00:17:19.317 --> 00:17:20.792
Keeps out demons.

00:17:21.106 --> 00:17:22.231
Demons, we know.

00:17:22.377 --> 00:17:23.471
Well, then,

00:17:23.756 --> 00:17:24.691
Keep it.

00:17:25.236 --> 00:17:27.272
Maybe it'll do you some good.

00:17:30.567 --> 00:17:32.463
4 minutes left.

00:17:35.535 --> 00:17:36.983
Mr. Darrow...

00:17:37.708 --> 00:17:40.721
We know you're in trouble.
Yeah, that you got yourself into.

00:17:41.966 --> 00:17:44.363
But it's not hopeless, all right?

00:17:44.845 --> 00:17:46.231
There's got to be something we can do.

00:17:46.235 --> 00:17:47.092
Listen,

00:17:47.507 --> 00:17:49.461
I get that you boys want to help,

00:17:50.555 --> 00:17:55.211
But sometimes a person makes their bed
and they just got to lie down in it.

00:17:58.297 --> 00:18:01.071
I'm the one called that
demon in the first place.

00:18:01.727 --> 00:18:03.541
What'd you do it for? I was weak.

00:18:04.715 --> 00:18:06.491
I mean, who don't want to be great?

00:18:07.227 --> 00:18:09.571
Who don't want their
life to mean something?

00:18:11.566 --> 00:18:12.440
I just...

00:18:13.938 --> 00:18:16.101
I just never thought about the price.

00:18:16.425 --> 00:18:17.353
Was it worth it?

00:18:17.357 --> 00:18:18.600
Hell, no

00:18:19.576 --> 00:18:21.293
Course, I asked for talent.

00:18:21.765 --> 00:18:23.533
Should have gone for fame.

00:18:24.907 --> 00:18:26.740
I'm still broke...

00:18:27.275 --> 00:18:28.501
And lonely.

00:18:28.695 --> 00:18:31.593
Just now I got this pile of
paintings don't nobody want.

00:18:34.036 --> 00:18:35.852
That wasn't the worst.

00:18:39.597 --> 00:18:40.551
Go on.

00:18:41.936 --> 00:18:43.500
Demon didn't leave.

00:18:43.898 --> 00:18:45.412
I never counted on that.

00:18:45.495 --> 00:18:48.962
After our deal was done, the damn
thing stayed at Lloyd's for a week,

00:18:49.255 --> 00:18:50.493
Just chatting,

00:18:51.067 --> 00:18:52.721
Making more deals.

00:18:54.128 --> 00:18:55.873
I tried to warn folks, but

00:18:56.468 --> 00:18:58.323
Who gonna listen to an old drunk?

00:18:58.327 --> 00:18:59.671
How many others are there?

00:19:00.095 --> 00:19:01.521
This architect,

00:19:01.998 --> 00:19:05.170
A doctor lady. I kept up with
them. They've been in the papers.

00:19:06.926 --> 00:19:08.611
At least they got famous.

00:19:09.776 --> 00:19:11.460
Who else, George? Come on, think.

00:19:11.945 --> 00:19:13.241
Oh, one more.

00:19:14.987 --> 00:19:16.383
Uh, nice guy, too.

00:19:18.006 --> 00:19:18.930
Hudson,

00:19:19.647 --> 00:19:20.881
Evan I think.

00:19:21.758 --> 00:19:23.571
I don't know what he asked for.

00:19:24.906 --> 00:19:26.352
Don't matter now.

00:19:26.365 --> 00:19:27.740
We're done for.

00:19:28.776 --> 00:19:29.780
No.

00:19:30.287 --> 00:19:32.251
No, there's got to be
a way. You don't get it.

00:19:32.705 --> 00:19:34.151
I don't want a way.

00:19:34.778 --> 00:19:37.550
Look, you don't... I called that thing!

00:19:37.848 --> 00:19:39.591
I brought it on myself!

00:19:41.226 --> 00:19:42.631
I brought it on them.

00:19:44.157 --> 00:19:46.071
I'm going to hell,

00:19:46.076 --> 00:19:47.402
One way or another.

00:19:49.298 --> 00:19:51.452
All I want is to
finish my last painting.

00:19:52.208 --> 00:19:54.131
Day or two, I'm done.

00:19:54.638 --> 00:19:57.102
I'm just trying to
hold him off till then,

00:19:58.236 --> 00:19:59.773
Buy a little time.

00:20:00.926 --> 00:20:04.352
Okay, boys, time you went. Go
help somebody that wants help.

00:20:04.355 --> 00:20:06.361
We can't just... Get out!

00:20:07.108 --> 00:20:08.432
I got work to do.

00:20:09.225 --> 00:20:11.071
You don't really want to die.

00:20:12.327 --> 00:20:13.383
I don't?

00:20:20.517 --> 00:20:21.773
I'm tired.

00:20:57.986 --> 00:20:59.021
Evan?

00:20:59.258 --> 00:21:01.282
Are you spying on the neighbors?

00:21:02.148 --> 00:21:03.672
No, I, uh,

00:21:03.677 --> 00:21:06.062
I thought I heard something
in the yard, but it's nothing.

00:21:07.545 --> 00:21:08.783
You all ready to go?

00:21:08.797 --> 00:21:12.612
You know, if I didn't know better, I'd
say that you want me out of the house.

00:21:13.245 --> 00:21:15.621
Of course not. It's just, you've...

00:21:15.826 --> 00:21:18.323
You've barely seen your
sister since she had the baby.

00:21:18.328 --> 00:21:19.932
Well, what are you
going to do all weekend?

00:21:21.357 --> 00:21:24.863
Um, not much. I got some bills to pay.

00:21:29.827 --> 00:21:31.323
Come here.

00:21:35.548 --> 00:21:36.603
I'll miss you.

00:21:36.606 --> 00:21:37.692
You better.

00:21:41.455 --> 00:21:42.762
You know I love you, right?

00:21:43.225 --> 00:21:44.200
Forever.

00:21:45.147 --> 00:21:47.143
Of course. Evan, are you okay?

00:21:48.066 --> 00:21:49.171
Yeah.

00:21:50.717 --> 00:21:52.201
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:21:53.387 --> 00:21:54.523
Now, get going.

00:21:56.797 --> 00:21:58.433
Okay, I'll call you when I get there.

00:22:00.758 --> 00:22:01.932
Hey, sweetie?

00:22:09.635 --> 00:22:10.871
I love you, too.

00:22:22.817 --> 00:22:24.382
Yes? Evan Hudson?

00:22:24.386 --> 00:22:25.130
Yeah.

00:22:25.135 --> 00:22:26.963
You ever been to a bar called Lloyd's?

00:22:27.057 --> 00:22:28.753
Would have been about 10 years ago.

00:22:30.487 --> 00:22:32.842
Come on, we're not demons.

00:22:34.646 --> 00:22:36.043
Any other bright ideas?

00:23:02.488 --> 00:23:03.222
Evan?

00:23:03.226 --> 00:23:04.201
Please!

00:23:04.806 --> 00:23:05.790
Don't hurt me.

00:23:05.798 --> 00:23:08.102
We're not gonna hurt you, all
right? We're here to help you.

00:23:08.308 --> 00:23:10.152
We know all about the
genius deal you made.

00:23:10.607 --> 00:23:11.473
What?

00:23:12.075 --> 00:23:13.523
How? Doesn't matter.

00:23:14.075 --> 00:23:15.543
All that matters is
we're trying to stop it.

00:23:15.546 --> 00:23:17.382
How do I know you're not
lying? Well, you don't.

00:23:17.385 --> 00:23:19.322
But you're kind of running low
on options, there, buddy boy.

00:23:25.375 --> 00:23:26.381
Can you stop it?

00:23:26.385 --> 00:23:27.251
Don't know.

00:23:27.406 --> 00:23:28.550
We'll try.

00:23:30.456 --> 00:23:31.653
I don't wanna die.

00:23:31.848 --> 00:23:33.533
Of course you don't. Not now. Dean...

00:23:33.778 --> 00:23:35.542
Stop. What'd you ask for, anyway, Ev?

00:23:35.548 --> 00:23:36.272
Huh?

00:23:36.917 --> 00:23:39.291
Never need viagra, bowl
a perfect game, what?

00:23:42.417 --> 00:23:43.442
My wife.

00:23:45.267 --> 00:23:47.670
Right, getting the girl.
That's worth a trip to hell for.

00:23:47.677 --> 00:23:49.251
Dean, stop. No.

00:23:50.585 --> 00:23:51.793
He's right. I made the deal.

00:23:54.115 --> 00:23:55.953
Nobody twisted my arm. That, uh,

00:23:56.466 --> 00:23:57.400
Woman,

00:23:58.556 --> 00:24:01.540
Or whatever she was, at the bar, she
said I could have anything I wanted.

00:24:01.547 --> 00:24:03.581
I thought she was nuts, at first, but...

00:24:09.208 --> 00:24:10.331
I don't know. I was...

00:24:11.507 --> 00:24:12.651
I was desperate.

00:24:13.378 --> 00:24:14.292
Desperate?

00:24:20.796 --> 00:24:22.292
Julie  was dying.

00:24:27.886 --> 00:24:29.100
You did it to save her?

00:24:31.796 --> 00:24:33.583
She had cancer. They
had stopped treatment.

00:24:33.596 --> 00:24:36.051
They were moving her into
hospice. They kept saying,

00:24:36.776 --> 00:24:38.152
"Matter of days".

00:24:40.806 --> 00:24:42.043
So, yeah, I made the deal...

00:24:42.577 --> 00:24:43.833
And I'd do it again.

00:24:44.198 --> 00:24:45.842
I'd have died for her on the spot.

00:24:50.535 --> 00:24:52.011
Did you ever think
about her in all this?

00:24:52.016 --> 00:24:53.510
I did this for her.

00:24:53.518 --> 00:24:54.752
You sure about that?

00:24:56.567 --> 00:24:58.052
I think you did it for yourself...

00:24:59.446 --> 00:25:00.972
So you wouldn't have
to live without her.

00:25:02.477 --> 00:25:04.561
But, guess what, she's gonna
have to live without you now.

00:25:07.987 --> 00:25:10.003
What if she knew how much it cost?

00:25:11.407 --> 00:25:13.133
What if she knew it cost your soul?

00:25:13.578 --> 00:25:14.841
How do you think she'd feel?

00:25:15.918 --> 00:25:17.861
Okay, that's enough. Evan,

00:25:18.027 --> 00:25:19.220
Sit tight, all right?

00:25:19.388 --> 00:25:20.600
We're gonna figure this out.

00:25:29.427 --> 00:25:31.303
You all right? Why wouldn't I be?

00:25:32.825 --> 00:25:34.002
Hey, I got an idea.

00:25:35.117 --> 00:25:36.830
You throw George's
hoodoo at that hellhound,

00:25:36.838 --> 00:25:38.661
Keep it away from Evan
as long as you can.

00:25:39.328 --> 00:25:41.250
I'm gonna go to the crossroads
and summon the demon.

00:25:41.257 --> 00:25:42.130
Summon...

00:25:42.628 --> 00:25:43.600
Are you nuts?

00:25:44.056 --> 00:25:45.550
Maybe a little.

00:25:45.895 --> 00:25:47.223
But I can trap it.

00:25:47.385 --> 00:25:50.211
I can exorcise it and I can buy us time
to figure out something more permanent.

00:25:50.216 --> 00:25:52.592
Yeah, but how much time?
I don't know. A while.

00:25:52.815 --> 00:25:55.991
It's not easy for those suckers to claw their
way back from hell and into the sunshine.

00:25:55.995 --> 00:25:56.741
No.

00:25:56.745 --> 00:25:58.210
No way. Not allowed to say no, Sammy,

00:25:58.216 --> 00:26:00.470
Unless you got a better idea.
Dean, you can forget it, all right?

00:26:00.485 --> 00:26:02.153
I'm not letting you
summon that demon. Why not?

00:26:02.158 --> 00:26:04.192
Because I don't like where your
head is at right now. That's why not.

00:26:04.225 --> 00:26:05.973
What are you talking about?
You've been on edge ever since

00:26:05.977 --> 00:26:08.130
We found that crossroads,
Dean, and I think I know why.

00:26:08.146 --> 00:26:10.062
We don't have time for this. Dad.

00:26:12.075 --> 00:26:14.731
You think maybe dad made
one of these deals, huh?

00:26:17.216 --> 00:26:18.020
Hell,

00:26:18.068 --> 00:26:19.490
I've been thinking it.

00:26:20.097 --> 00:26:21.730
I'm sure you've been thinking it, too.

00:26:29.756 --> 00:26:31.021
It fits, doesn't it?

00:26:32.526 --> 00:26:34.330
I'm alive, dad's dead.

00:26:34.557 --> 00:26:36.163
Yellow-Eyed demon was involved.

00:26:38.305 --> 00:26:39.423
What if he did?

00:26:40.925 --> 00:26:42.212
What if he struck a deal?

00:26:43.716 --> 00:26:45.091
My life for his soul.

00:26:48.665 --> 00:26:50.702
<i>Hey, guys, I think I
hear it! It's outside!</i>

00:26:50.898 --> 00:26:52.513
Just keep him alive, okay?

00:26:53.848 --> 00:26:55.172
Dean? Go!

00:27:21.205 --> 00:27:22.153
So,

00:27:22.427 --> 00:27:25.281
What brings a guy like
you to a place like this?

00:27:27.986 --> 00:27:29.221
You called me?

00:27:29.465 --> 00:27:30.882
I'm just glad it worked.

00:27:32.706 --> 00:27:33.830
First time?

00:27:35.415 --> 00:27:36.551
You could say that.

00:27:36.957 --> 00:27:38.500
Oh, come on, now.

00:27:38.895 --> 00:27:40.742
Don't sell yourself short.

00:27:41.068 --> 00:27:43.462
I know all about you, Dean Winchester.

00:27:46.225 --> 00:27:47.743
So you know who I am.

00:27:47.977 --> 00:27:49.362
I get the newsletter.

00:27:49.505 --> 00:27:51.341
Well, don't keep me in suspense.

00:27:51.855 --> 00:27:53.033
What have you heard?

00:27:53.567 --> 00:27:54.652
Well,

00:27:54.755 --> 00:27:56.871
I heard you were handsome.

00:27:57.706 --> 00:27:58.980
You're just edible.

00:28:00.127 --> 00:28:02.222
What can I do for you, Dean?

00:28:04.816 --> 00:28:06.801
Maybe we should do this in my car.

00:28:07.525 --> 00:28:08.671
Nice and private.

00:28:08.676 --> 00:28:10.440
Sounds good to me.

00:28:26.886 --> 00:28:29.480
What is that stuff? Goofer dust.

00:28:29.536 --> 00:28:30.881
Are you serious?

00:28:31.435 --> 00:28:33.213
Yeah. Afraid so.

00:28:34.045 --> 00:28:36.750
Look, believe me, don't
believe me... Whatever you want.

00:28:36.757 --> 00:28:38.271
Just whatever you do,

00:28:38.465 --> 00:28:40.602
Stay inside this circle, all right?

00:28:41.848 --> 00:28:44.122
So, I was hoping we could strike a deal.

00:28:44.128 --> 00:28:45.720
That's what I do.

00:28:45.986 --> 00:28:48.802
I want Evan Hudson
released from his contract.

00:28:49.696 --> 00:28:51.540
So sorry, darling.

00:28:51.848 --> 00:28:53.761
That's not negotiable.

00:28:54.027 --> 00:28:55.721
I'll make it worth your while.

00:28:56.058 --> 00:28:57.472
Oh, really?

00:28:57.755 --> 00:28:59.640
What are you offering? Me.

00:29:02.686 --> 00:29:04.782
Well, well, well.

00:29:05.636 --> 00:29:08.083
You'd sacrifice your
life for someone else's.

00:29:09.347 --> 00:29:11.181
Like father, like son.

00:29:18.256 --> 00:29:19.903
That's the last of it.

00:29:20.766 --> 00:29:23.680
You did know about
your dad's deal, right?

00:29:23.807 --> 00:29:25.520
His life for yours.

00:29:27.295 --> 00:29:29.833
Oh, I didn't make the deal myself, but,

00:29:29.988 --> 00:29:32.250
Boy, I wish I had.

00:29:38.017 --> 00:29:39.131
After you.

00:29:39.135 --> 00:29:40.782
Such a gentleman.

00:29:45.385 --> 00:29:46.663
A devil's trap?

00:29:46.927 --> 00:29:49.372
You've got to be kidding me.

00:29:50.086 --> 00:29:50.923
What?

00:29:50.927 --> 00:29:52.003
You hear that?

00:29:52.325 --> 00:29:53.571
No. Where?

00:29:55.866 --> 00:29:57.490
Right outside the door.

00:30:10.786 --> 00:30:12.152
Just don't move, all right?

00:30:12.156 --> 00:30:13.600
Stay where you are.

00:30:17.247 --> 00:30:19.603
You stupid, stupid...

00:30:20.148 --> 00:30:22.061
I should rip you limb from limb.

00:30:22.068 --> 00:30:23.262
Take your best shot.

00:30:25.888 --> 00:30:27.130
No,

00:30:27.716 --> 00:30:29.160
I don't think so.

00:30:29.755 --> 00:30:31.561
I'm not gonna put you
out of your misery.

00:30:31.567 --> 00:30:32.481
Yeah? Why not?

00:30:32.495 --> 00:30:34.441
'Cause your misery is the whole point.

00:30:34.547 --> 00:30:36.451
It's too much fun to watch.

00:30:37.437 --> 00:30:39.930
Knowing how your daddy died for you,

00:30:39.938 --> 00:30:41.732
How he sold his soul.

00:30:41.857 --> 00:30:42.972
I mean,

00:30:42.977 --> 00:30:44.483
That's got to hurt.

00:30:47.097 --> 00:30:49.021
He's all you ever think about.

00:30:49.025 --> 00:30:51.051
You wake up, and your first thought is

00:30:51.056 --> 00:30:53.103
"I can't do this anymore".

00:30:53.348 --> 00:30:55.310
You're all lit up with pain.

00:30:55.508 --> 00:30:59.610
I mean, you loved him so
much. And it's all your fault.

00:31:01.768 --> 00:31:03.400
You blew it, Dean.

00:31:03.738 --> 00:31:05.352
I could have given you what you need.

00:31:05.356 --> 00:31:06.760
What do I need?

00:31:08.227 --> 00:31:09.440
Your father.

00:31:11.097 --> 00:31:12.851
I could have brought him back.

00:31:14.215 --> 00:31:15.541
Your loss.

00:31:16.085 --> 00:31:17.331
See ya, Dean.

00:31:17.335 --> 00:31:19.692
I wish you a nice, long life.

00:31:29.418 --> 00:31:30.402
Hold on.

00:31:53.185 --> 00:31:54.342
Do you still hear it?

00:31:54.987 --> 00:31:55.883
No.

00:31:56.278 --> 00:31:57.320
Is it over?

00:32:03.936 --> 00:32:05.182
It's here!

00:32:11.866 --> 00:32:16.081
You're lucky I've got a soft spot
for lost puppies and long faces.

00:32:17.438 --> 00:32:19.841
I just can't leave you like this.

00:32:20.135 --> 00:32:21.452
Besides,

00:32:21.468 --> 00:32:23.783
You didn't call me here
to bargain for Evan.

00:32:23.945 --> 00:32:25.181
Not really.

00:32:25.196 --> 00:32:26.802
Can you bring him back?

00:32:27.546 --> 00:32:28.772
My dad?

00:32:29.627 --> 00:32:31.121
Of course I can,

00:32:31.136 --> 00:32:32.900
Just as he was.

00:32:33.767 --> 00:32:36.192
Your dad would live
a long, natural life,

00:32:36.338 --> 00:32:37.961
Like he was meant to.

00:32:38.526 --> 00:32:40.760
That's a promise. What about me?

00:32:40.766 --> 00:32:42.701
I could give you 10 years,

00:32:42.708 --> 00:32:45.572
10 long, good years with him.

00:32:45.777 --> 00:32:47.393
That's a lifetime.

00:32:47.618 --> 00:32:49.442
The family could be together again.

00:32:49.457 --> 00:32:51.771
John, Dean, Sammy...

00:32:52.165 --> 00:32:55.080
The Winchester boys all reunited.

00:32:59.648 --> 00:33:00.420
Look,

00:33:00.708 --> 00:33:02.750
Your dad is supposed to be alive.

00:33:03.715 --> 00:33:05.341
You're supposed to be dead.

00:33:06.148 --> 00:33:08.223
So, we'll just set things straight,

00:33:08.677 --> 00:33:11.011
Put things back in their natural order,

00:33:11.336 --> 00:33:13.823
And you get 10 extra years on top.

00:33:14.317 --> 00:33:16.053
That's a bonus.

00:33:24.915 --> 00:33:26.030
You think you could...

00:33:32.587 --> 00:33:34.181
Throw in a set of steak knives?

00:33:36.227 --> 00:33:39.491
You know, this smartass
self-Sefense mechanism of yours...

00:33:46.646 --> 00:33:48.000
Dean...

00:33:48.006 --> 00:33:49.511
Now you're really trapped.

00:33:50.526 --> 00:33:51.401
That's got to hurt.

00:33:51.408 --> 00:33:53.991
Let me out now.

00:33:53.995 --> 00:33:54.751
Sure.

00:33:54.756 --> 00:33:57.320
We just got to make a
little deal here first.

00:33:57.325 --> 00:33:59.103
You call off your hellhound

00:33:59.237 --> 00:34:00.541
And let Evan go.

00:34:01.368 --> 00:34:02.592
Then I'll let you go.

00:34:03.185 --> 00:34:05.753
I can't break a binding contract.

00:34:06.776 --> 00:34:08.680
And by "can't," you
mean "don't want to"?

00:34:09.895 --> 00:34:11.173
Last chance.

00:34:12.017 --> 00:34:14.620
Evan and his wife get to
live to a ripe old age.

00:34:15.195 --> 00:34:16.301
Going...

00:34:16.776 --> 00:34:18.511
Going... Let's talk about this.

00:34:18.516 --> 00:34:19.431
Okay, gone.

00:34:22.765 --> 00:34:23.951
Stay inside the circle!

00:34:33.816 --> 00:34:35.370
Come on, Dean...

00:34:37.277 --> 00:34:38.293
What are you doing?

00:34:38.378 --> 00:34:40.022
Oh, you're just gonna
go on a little trip.

00:34:42.318 --> 00:34:43.470
Way down south.

00:34:43.477 --> 00:34:45.441
Look, forget Evan. Think of your dad.

00:34:49.476 --> 00:34:50.731
Regna terrae,

00:34:50.975 --> 00:34:53.350
Cantate deo, psallite domino.

00:34:53.807 --> 00:34:56.103
Qui fertur super caelum caeli

00:34:56.117 --> 00:34:57.681
Ad orientem,

00:34:57.688 --> 00:35:01.120
Ecce dabit vocem suam, vocem virtutis.

00:35:01.128 --> 00:35:03.483
Tribuite virtutem deo.

00:35:03.487 --> 00:35:06.503
Qui fertur super caelum
caeli ad orientem,

00:35:11.548 --> 00:35:13.180
Circle's broken! Come on!

00:35:19.266 --> 00:35:20.510
Omnis fallaciae,

00:35:20.828 --> 00:35:22.731
Libera nos domine.

00:35:28.046 --> 00:35:30.223
Hostis humanae salutis.

00:35:33.126 --> 00:35:34.541
Wait!

00:35:59.118 --> 00:36:00.500
What the hell was that for?

00:36:00.627 --> 00:36:02.031
Sealing the deal.

00:36:02.036 --> 00:36:03.311
I usually like to be warned

00:36:03.317 --> 00:36:05.301
Before I'm violated with demon tongue.

00:36:05.377 --> 00:36:07.083
Evan Hudson is free.

00:36:07.356 --> 00:36:10.531
He and his wife will live long
lives. How do I know you're not lying?

00:36:10.536 --> 00:36:12.590
My word is my bond. Oh, really?

00:36:12.595 --> 00:36:14.361
It is when I make a deal.

00:36:14.645 --> 00:36:16.113
It's the rules.

00:36:17.046 --> 00:36:18.650
You got what you wanted.

00:36:19.055 --> 00:36:20.441
Now let me go.

00:36:31.417 --> 00:36:33.682
You're gonna double-Cross me?

00:36:33.758 --> 00:36:36.122
Funny how I'm the trustworthy one.

00:36:38.267 --> 00:36:39.851
You know,

00:36:40.075 --> 00:36:42.650
You renege, send me to hell,

00:36:42.668 --> 00:36:45.092
Sooner or later I'm gonna climb out, and

00:36:45.096 --> 00:36:47.931
Skinning Evan Hudson will
be the first thing that I do.

00:37:06.368 --> 00:37:07.540
I got to tell you,

00:37:07.965 --> 00:37:10.252
You would have never pulled
that stunt if you knew.

00:37:10.256 --> 00:37:11.051
Knew what?

00:37:11.398 --> 00:37:13.113
Where your dad is.

00:37:13.648 --> 00:37:15.232
You should have made that deal.

00:37:15.937 --> 00:37:17.832
See, people talk about hell,

00:37:18.077 --> 00:37:19.391
But it's just a word.

00:37:19.596 --> 00:37:22.240
Doesn't even come close
to describing the real...

00:37:22.246 --> 00:37:24.931
Shut your mouth, bitch! If
you could see your poor daddy,

00:37:24.938 --> 00:37:27.122
Hear the sounds he makes
'cause he can't even scream.

00:37:27.137 --> 00:37:28.690
How about I send you back there?

00:37:39.008 --> 00:37:39.763
What?

00:37:41.466 --> 00:37:43.033
How did I get here?

00:37:48.416 --> 00:37:51.643
<i>"Key to the Highway" by Big Bill Broonzy</i>

00:37:56.205 --> 00:37:57.873
Demons lie all the time, right?

00:37:57.938 --> 00:37:59.220
Maybe she was lying.

00:37:59.226 --> 00:38:01.273
Come on, is that really what you think?

00:38:04.176 --> 00:38:05.752
How could he do it?

00:38:05.756 --> 00:38:07.970
He did it for you. Exactly.

00:38:08.205 --> 00:38:09.791
How am I supposed to live with that?

00:38:11.628 --> 00:38:13.200
You know, the thought of him,

00:38:15.085 --> 00:38:16.992
Wherever he is right now...

00:38:18.165 --> 00:38:20.563
I mean, he spent his
whole life chasing that

00:38:21.306 --> 00:38:23.262
Yellow-Eyed son of a bitch.

00:38:23.556 --> 00:38:25.512
He should have gone out fighting.

00:38:27.567 --> 00:38:29.643
That was supposed to be his legacy,

00:38:29.645 --> 00:38:31.083
You know?

00:38:32.568 --> 00:38:34.893
Not bargaining with the damn thing.

00:38:37.197 --> 00:38:38.331
Not this.

00:38:38.335 --> 00:38:40.843
How many people do you
think dad saved total?

00:38:40.847 --> 00:38:43.772
That's not the point,
Sam. Evan Hudson is safe

00:38:43.905 --> 00:38:45.873
Because of what dad taught us.

00:38:46.896 --> 00:38:48.531
That's his legacy, Dean.

00:38:49.925 --> 00:38:51.362
Now, we're still here, man,

00:38:51.365 --> 00:38:53.063
So we got to keep going.

00:38:53.895 --> 00:38:55.123
For him.

00:39:01.648 --> 00:39:02.743
Dean? Yeah?

00:39:02.746 --> 00:39:04.643
When you were trapping
that demon, you weren't...

00:39:06.528 --> 00:39:08.373
I mean, it was all a trick, right?

00:39:08.467 --> 00:39:11.500
You never considered actually
making that deal, right?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.500
